# Fly Sprites's settings (`metacomputer vm create NAME --on sprites` writes them to config/vms/NAME.env), as comments:
# nothing here is read as a setting; config/defaults.env has the defaults every computer shares. Its docs: docs/sprites.md.
#   PLACE=sprites, PROVIDER=sprites, TRANSPORT=sprite
#   SPRITE_ORG               the Fly organization it's made in (vm create --org, or SPRITES_ORG)
#   SPRITE_NAME              the Sprite (the computer's name by default; vm create --sprite)
#   SPRITE_CLI               Fly's sprite command, when it isn't on your PATH or in ~/.local/bin
#   IDLE_STOP=off            it sleeps by itself about 10 s after nothing is connected; SIZE and REGION don't apply
#   EGRESS                   internet or off: Fly's network policy, outside the computer (net allow lists names)
# This checkout's settings (config/local.env):
#   SPRITES_ORG              the organization vm create --on sprites and cloud ... sprites use when --org isn't given
# Its credentials: none in the environment. Fly's sprite command keeps its own sign-in (sprite login).
